# Build output. `/ticfac` is the built binary; `!/ticfac/` un-ignores the
# directory of the same name (SPEC §12 Phase 4: the factory worker bundle
# moved there as ticfac/cloudflare), so a new file under it can never be
# silently skipped by `git add`. `/dist/` is goreleaser's output — the
# snapshot releases a developer cuts locally land there with every platform
# binary and archive (tick 4yb).
/ticfac
!/ticfac/
/dist/
/bin/

# Go test and coverage artefacts
*.test
*.out
coverage.*

# Hegel's example database: the Rust engine writes its generated cases beside
# the working directory of the test binary, so every package with a Hegel
# property test grows a .hegel/ when its suite runs (tick 89g). It is exhaust
# the way coverage files are — a run's own gate leaves it in the checkout, and
# without this line it is a dirty tree a later `git add -A` sweeps up.
.hegel/

# BEGIN ticfac run state
# .ticfac/runs/** is COMMITTED — it is the run's durable record (SPEC 10.4),
# and durable means pushed on origin. Only these two are exhaust:
.ticfac/.index.json
.ticfac/logs/
# END ticfac run state
